-I6-J6). Since F6 and K6 are empty, this forms an "Open 4", which is an immediate win (White cannot block both ends).\n\nReason: White threatens an immediate win at G10. Black must play a sequence of forcing moves (checks) to prevent this. Black can play H6 (creating a vertical 4), then I6 (creating a diagonal 4), then J6 (creating another diagonal 4). These moves force White to respond defensively. This setup places three Black stones on row 6 (H6, I6, J6). Black can then play G6 to create an unstoppable Open 4. H6 is the first move in this winning sequence.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "H", "row": 6}'}
